KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--unwindset 'ns::fill(ptr_signed_int,struct_tag(identifier=ns::tag-it)).0:1' --unwinding-assertions
^\[fill\.unwind\.0\] line \d+ unwinding assertion loop 0: FAILURE$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
invalid loop identifier
--
--unwindset splits its argument at every comma
(cmdline.get_comma_separated_values), so this entry becomes
`ns::fill(ptr_signed_int' and `struct_tag(identifier=ns::tag-it)).0:1'; the
first is rejected with "invalid loop identifier ns:".
